# One line-ending convention in the repository, on every platform.
#
# Without this a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites every text
# file to CRLF, and the release fails on its own gates: the Agent Skills index
# pins a sha256 over the bytes of SKILL.md, `.bun-version` is compared as an
# exact string, and `assertMarkdownRelease` compares `public/` against `dist/`
# byte for byte. Those checks are correct — the checkout was the problem.
#
# `text=auto` still lets Git decide what is text; `eol=lf` only fixes what
# lands in the working tree for the files it decides are.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched: rewriting a byte here corrupts the asset, and for the icons it
# breaks the digest the release carries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
